# The Study of Consumer Behavior and Social Validity: An Essential Partnership for Applied Behavior Analysis.

**Authors:** Schwartz, Ilene S.

## Abstract
This article challenges applied behavior analysts to use their knowledge of consumer behavior and effective educational strategies to provide consumers with useful information, thereby enabling them to make informed decisions. This will decrease the misconceptions that many consumers have about behavior analysis, thus improving the social validity of behavioral interventions. (JDD)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ432909

